# L §4.2 Key arithmetic: "y - 1, m + 12 ... A result outside the index is refused at that key (RUN-KEY) where it
# stands in a key position. In a value position a key of an integer index is an int, so k - 1 at the first key is
# plain int arithmetic."  "The difference of two keys of one ordered index, k1 - k2, is an int: the difference of
# their positions (for an integer or period index, of the integers or periods)."  Date arithmetic: "month ± int
# by months, year ± int by years".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index ks = 1..3
index gs = [g1, g2, g3]

ask q1: k - 1 for k in ks where pos(k) == 1
ask q2: count(g in gs where g - g1 == 1), 2026-03 + 1, year_of(2026-05-10) - 1
=== expect
q1 (k = 1): 0
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: (1, 2026-04, 2025)
  cut 2026-12-31
